#
# DEVS:Internet/hosts
#
# Names this Amiga knows without asking a name server.  The standard /etc
# layout: an address, the real name, then any number of nicknames.
#
#     <address>   <name>   [nickname ...]
#
# '#' starts a comment.  Columns are separated by any run of spaces or tabs.
#
# AmiTCP's habit of putting the word HOST in front of the address is
# accepted too, so an AmiTCP netdb-myhost can be dropped in here unchanged.
#
# If this file is missing entirely, the stack falls back to a built-in table
# with just localhost in it, so the machine is never completely nameless.
#

127.0.0.1	localhost loopback

# Your own machines, so they work without a name server:
#
#192.168.1.1	router gateway
#192.168.1.10	amiga
#192.168.1.20	fileserver nas
